#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:1
msgid ""
"Masterclass 22.01: Funnel Metadynamics (FM): predicting ligand binding "
"models, binding free energies and kinetics"
msgstr ""
"Masterclass 22.01：Funnel Metadynamics (FM)：Ligand 結合モデル・自由エネルギー・Kinetics の予測"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:3
msgid "Origin"
msgstr "作成について"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:5
msgid ""
"This tutorial is a reworked version of the masterclass by Stefano Raniolo "
"and Vittorio Limongelli from the 31st of January, 2022"
msgstr ""
"2022年1月31日の Stefano Raniolo と Vittorio Limongelli の Masterclass を再構成した "
"Tutorial です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:7
msgid "Aims"
msgstr "目的"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:9
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, it will be possible to learn the basics of Funnel "
"Metadynamics (FM), how to set up a FM simulation, and we will see few "
"analyses that are routinely carried out to check for convergence in the "
"calculation. Users might find helpful to read the FM protocol "
"[pubblication](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41596-020-0342-4) in "
"advance."
msgstr ""
"FM の基礎、設定、日常的な収束確認の解析を学びます。事前に [Protocol "
"論文](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41596-020-0342-4) を読むと役立ちます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:11
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr "到達目標"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:13
msgid "Once you have completed this tutorial you will be able to:"
msgstr "完了すると次ができます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:15
msgid "Set up a FM simulation using one of the developed tools."
msgstr "用意したツールで FM を設定する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:16
msgid ""
"Use PLUMED and GROMACS to run FM simulations on a paradigmatic system "
"(benzamidine/trypsin)."
msgstr "PLUMED と GROMACS で代表系 Benzamidine/Trypsin の FM を実行する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:17
msgid ""
"Analyse a FM simulation, checking for convergence and calculating the free-"
"energy estimate. It addition these concepts also shown in the Masterclass of"
" 2022, we will also describe a procedure to estimate kinetic constants "
"starting from the information obtained from FM."
msgstr ""
"FM を解析し、収束と自由エネルギー推定を確認する。2022年 Masterclass の内容に加え、FM の情報から Kinetic Constant"
" を推定する手順も説明します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:19
msgid "Recommended PLUMED setup"
msgstr "推奨 PLUMED 設定"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:21
msgid ""
"Although it is possible to use the most basic implementation of PLUMED + "
"GROMACS to follow this tutorial, it is suggested for the user to compile "
"using the MPI library and possibly run the FM simulation on a HPC system."
msgstr "基本的な PLUMED + GROMACS でも実行できますが、MPI 対応ビルドと、可能なら HPC を推奨します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:23
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "資料"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:25
msgid ""
"The inputs that are required for the tutorial can in part be found in "
"[Github](https://github.com/h2nch2co2h/masterclass-22-1.git). You can clone "
"this repository locally in a machine using the following command:"
msgstr ""
"入力の一部は [GitHub](https://github.com/h2nch2co2h/masterclass-22-1.git) にあり、次で "
"Clone できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:32
msgid ""
"**Simulation of the benzamidine/trypsin system has been carried out with "
"GROMACS v5.14 and a customised version of PLUMED v2.6.**"
msgstr "**Benzamidine/Trypsin は GROMACS v5.14 と独自版 PLUMED v2.6 で実行しました。**"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:34
msgid "Overview of the tutorial"
msgstr "構成"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:36
msgid "This tutorial can be divided mainly in three main sectors:"
msgstr "主に3部分です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:38
msgid ""
"pre-processing: setup of the FM simulation and generation of necessary "
"parameters and inputs;"
msgstr "前処理：設定とパラメータ・入力の生成。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:39
msgid "simulation: running a FM simulation;"
msgstr "シミュレーション：FM の実行。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:40
msgid ""
"post-processing: analyse the output of a FM simulation to know "
"thermodynamics and kinetics of a binding mechanism."
msgstr "後処理：結合機構の Thermodynamics と Kinetics の解析。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:42
msgid ""
"We will focalise on the first and last points, leaving running the "
"simulation as a user responsibility. This is done because a FM simulation "
"can last for days (depending on the hardware where the simulation is being "
"run) if convergence is sought after. In case the user should feel unsure "
"about metadynamics parameters or launching it, it is suggested to follow the"
" this [tutorial](https://www.plumed-"
"tutorials.org/lessons/21/004/data/NAVIGATION.html). To save up time, we also"
" provide few outputs in case the user would like to skip the simulation "
"phase and directly perform the analyses."
msgstr ""
"前処理と後処理に注目し、実行は各自で行います。収束には Hardware により数日かかるためです。Metadynamics "
"パラメータや起動に不安があれば [この Tutorial](https://www.plumed-"
"tutorials.org/lessons/21/004/data/NAVIGATION.html) "
"を参照してください。実行を省き直接解析できる出力例も用意します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:46
msgid "Exercises"
msgstr "演習"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:48
msgid ""
"FM simulations can be run from a correctly minimized and thermalized system "
"and we are giving for granted that the user knows how to perform these "
"tasks. These are the only prerequisite and the tpr file provided is ready "
"for the production run. In case the user would like to apply the following "
"tutorial on a different complex than the benzamidine/trypsin system, we "
"highly recommend to start the pre-processing exercise from a structure that "
"underwent at least minimization and thermalization."
msgstr ""
"FM は正しく Minimization・Thermalization した系から始められ、それらの手順は既知とします。付属 tpr "
"は本計算用です。別の複合体に適用する場合も、少なくとも Minimization・Thermalization 後の構造から前処理を始めてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:50
msgid "Pre-processing exercise"
msgstr "前処理演習"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:52
msgid ""
"The first exercise will be to create a fitting funnel for the system at "
"hand. Similarly to the masterclass, we will use the benzamidine/trypsin "
"system. In general, coordinates and topology for the system should be "
"generated with the MD engine of one's choice, but in this tutorial we are "
"goinge to see examples using GROMACS. You can find coordinates and topology "
"for the benzamidine/trypsin system inside the data folder of Github."
msgstr ""
"まず系に適切な Funnel を作ります。Benzamidine/Trypsin を使います。座標・Topology は任意の MD "
"エンジンで作れますが、ここでは GROMACS を例にし、GitHub の data に用意しています。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:54
msgid ""
"At this point the user can decide to use the VMD plug-in or the Funnel "
"Metadynamics Pre-Processing Tool web-server. We will start here with the "
"former, if you wish to use the latter skip directly to point 18."
msgstr "VMD Plugin または Web Server を選べます。まず前者を説明します。後者なら手順18へ進んでください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:56
msgid ""
"Open VMD and load the coordinate file (start.gro). In general, this file "
"should be the output at the end of the thermalization process but, in case "
"of neccessity, also a pdb from the Protein DataBank can be used. Go to "
"\"Extensions\" and press \"Tk console\". Once the console has been opened "
"you can load the necessary libraries through the following commands:"
msgstr ""
"VMD に start.gro を読み込みます。通常は Thermalization 後の出力ですが、必要なら Protein Data Bank の "
"PDB も使えます。Extensions の Tk console を開き、次で必要な Library を読みます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:61
msgid ""
"At this point the interface for the FM pre-processing should be accessible "
"by calling in the terminal:"
msgstr "次を Console で呼ぶと前処理 Interface が開きます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:65
msgid "or"
msgstr "または"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:69
msgid ""
"At this point, the GUI should open and an orange funnel should appear in the"
" visualization window."
msgstr "GUI が開き、表示に橙の Funnel が現れるはずです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:71
msgid ""
"Now it is necessary to adapt the funnel shape, which is initialised with "
"standard values, to the system under study. The first thing to change are "
"the two points that define the axis of the funnel. In the visualization "
"wwindoww of VMD they correspond to two spheres, called A (in yellow) and B "
"(in green). Both points can be modified either by clicking an atom of the "
"system in the visualization window or by changing their Cartesian "
"coordinates in the interface. Starting with point A, select the option to "
"change it from the interface, click on the visualization window of VMD, "
"press the key 'p' and pick an atom of choice of the receptor. The funnel "
"should have changed direction. Do the same for point B. Adjust the funnel "
"axis until you reached a satisfactory coverage of the binding pocket with an"
" acceptable escape pathway. Alternatively, it is possible to change the "
"coordinate boxes of points A and B in the interface by typing a value in Å "
"or using the arrows to increment or decrement their Cartesian coordinates by"
" 0.1 Å. Pressing 'Enter', the value in the box will be read and the funnel "
"will be updated accordingly. During the funnel placement, it is possible to "
"switch between 'Invisible mode' and 'Transparent mode', which could help in "
"better selecting the direction. For the sake of this tutorial coordinates of"
" 4.724, 5.369, and 4.069 nm and 4.597, 5.721, 4.343 nm (for point A and B, "
"respectively) are good enough."
msgstr ""
"標準形の Funnel を系に合わせます。まず軸の2点 A（黄）・B（緑）を変えます。Interface で対象点を選び、表示をクリックして p "
"を押し、Receptor の原子を選ぶか、Cartesian 座標を直接変更します。両点を調整し、結合 Pocket を覆い、適切な Escape "
"Pathway を取る軸にします。座標欄は Å で入力するか、矢印で0.1 Å 刻みに変え、Enter で反映します。Invisible mode と "
"Transparent mode も選択に便利です。ここでは A=(4.724, 5.369, 4.069) nm、B=(4.597, 5.721, "
"4.343) nm で十分です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:73
msgid ""
"TO BE NOTED: when using the atom selector with the 'p' key, the system will "
"be constantly waiting for inputs to update point A or B. For this reason, we"
" suggest to always revert to the normal rotation mode of VMD after picking "
"an atom by pressing the 'r' key. This will avoid accidental replacement of "
"point A or B."
msgstr "注意：p による選択中は入力を待ち続けるため、選択後は r で通常の回転に戻し、A・B の誤変更を防いでください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:75
msgid ""
"Next step is to change the funnel shape to adapt to the benzamidine/trypsin "
"system. The 'Zcc' value regulates the switching point between the cone and "
"cylinder region of the funnel and should be selected so that the cone region"
" can include all the residues surrounding the target binding site. Once a "
"value has been selected, press 'Enter' to confirm the change. A value around"
" 1.8 nm should be enough."
msgstr ""
"Zcc は Cone と Cylinder の切替点です。Cone が結合部位周囲の全残基を含むよう選び、Enter で確定します。約1.8 nm "
"で十分です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:77
msgid ""
"TO BE NOTED: the funnel potential is applied on the center of mass (COM) of "
"the ligand; thus, only the ligand’s COM is kept inside the orange volume "
"during the simulation (large ligands might have part of their structure "
"outside the funnel without feeling any repulsion as long as their COM is "
"within the funnel volume)."
msgstr ""
"注意：Potential は Ligand の Center of Mass (COM) に作用します。COM だけが橙の領域内に保たれ、大きい "
"Ligand の一部が外に出ても COM が中なら反発はありません。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:79
msgid ""
"Together with Zcc, the cone region can be optimised by adjusting the "
"amplitude of the cone section in radians, which is regulated by the 'Alpha' "
"parameter. Greater values increase the explored region of the binding site. "
"Once a value has been selected, press 'Enter' to confirm the change. In this"
" case, a value of 0.55 is a good compromise."
msgstr ""
"Alpha は Cone の開きを radian で調整します。大きいほど結合部位の探索領域が広がります。Enter で確定します。0.55が妥当です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:81
msgid ""
"Last parameter to fine tune is the 'RCyl', which is the radius of the "
"cylinder section (in the unbound region). The radius value is set by default"
" to 1 Å. In most of the cases, the user does not need to change this value. "
"A larger radius implies a larger volume to explore by the ligand in the "
"unbound state and consequently a more time-consuming calculation. For the "
"tutorial, it is possible to leave the default value but the user can see how"
" the funnel changes increasing the cylinder radius. Always press 'Enter' to "
"finalise the new value."
msgstr ""
"RCyl は非結合 Cylinder の半径で、既定1 Å "
"は通常そのままで十分です。大きいほど非結合体積と計算時間が増えます。変更して形を見てもよいですが、ここでは既定を使えます。Enter で確定します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:83
msgid ""
"Once the funnel shape has been optimised, it is necessary to limit the "
"sampling of the funnel along the funnel axis and for this we wil use two "
"PLUMED walls. The first is a lower wall 'Low. Wall', which controls the "
"minimum value that can be sampled as projection of the ligand’s COM along "
"the funnel axis. A value of 0 corresponds to the position of point A, with "
"negative values going deeper in the conical region, whereas positive values "
"reduce the sampling to positions closer to the unbound state. A red sphere "
"in the visualization window shows its position relative to points A and B. "
"If the binding mode is not known, 'Low. Wall' should be defined so as to "
"ensure the full exploration of the binding site. A value of -0.3 nm should "
"suffice."
msgstr ""
"次に軸方向を2つの PLUMED Wall で制限します。Low. Wall は COM の軸射影の下限です。0は A、負は Cone "
"の深部、正は非結合側に近づきます。赤球で位置を示します。結合様式が不明なら部位全体を探索できるようにします。-0.3 nm で十分です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:85
msgid ""
"The second wall is called 'Up. Wall' and regulates the sampling on the "
"uppermost edge of the funnel, towards the cylinder region. This constraint "
"is set up to accelerate convergence and not waste time in the unbound "
"region. In general, this value should allow for the sampling of 2-3 Å inside"
" the cylinder region outside of the influence of the target (typically from "
"10 to 15 Å of the closest target atom). It is always computed with respect "
"to the distance from point A and, similarly to 'Low. Wall', it is defined by"
" a red sphere in the visualization window. In our case, anything close to "
"3.5 nm is sufficient to have an unbound region for benzamidine outside of "
"the trypsin influence."
msgstr ""
"Up. Wall は Cylinder 側の上限で、非結合領域に時間を費やしすぎず収束を速めます。通常、標的の影響外（最近原子から10〜15 Å）で "
"Cylinder 内2〜3 Å を探索できるようにします。A からの距離で定義し、赤球で示します。ここでは約3.5 nm で Benzamidine が"
" Trypsin の影響を離れられます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:87
msgid ""
"The bias imposed by the FM will be constructed as a grid and, as such, "
"requires lower and upper limits. The lower limit is called 'Min fps.lp' and "
"should be set at least 0.5 Å lower than the value of 'Low. Wall'."
msgstr "FM Bias は Grid なので上下限が必要です。Min fps.lp は Low. Wall より少なくとも0.5 Å 下にします。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:89
msgid ""
"Conversely, on the other side we have 'Max fps.lp', which should be set at "
"least 0.5 Å higher than the value of 'Up. Wall'."
msgstr "Max fps.lp は Up. Wall より少なくとも0.5 Å 上にします。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:91
msgid ""
"During the FM simulation it is possible that the simulation might stop due "
"to periodic-boundary-condition issues, which generally missplace the ligand "
"outside of the funnel grid. To counteract this, FM employes an anchor point,"
" which should be an atom of the target structure that is as close as "
"possible to the ligand both in the bound and in the unbound state. To select"
" it, click on the option to define the anchor and then press the key 'p' to "
"select an atom in the visualization window. For the sake of the tutorial, "
"the user can pick whichever atom outside of the trypsin binding pocket."
msgstr ""
"PBC により Ligand が Funnel Grid の外へ誤配置され、停止する場合があります。防ぐため、結合時・非結合時とも Ligand "
"にできる限り近い標的原子を Anchor とします。選択オプションを押し、p で原子を選びます。ここでは Trypsin Pocket "
"外の任意の原子でかまいません。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:93
msgid ""
"At this point, all necessary parameters for the funnel have been set and we "
"need to define the last parts to complete a working PLUMED input for FM. "
"Type in the box to the right of 'ID' the VMD identification number of the "
"structure you loaded. This number can be found on the left in the VMD main "
"menu where the structure file of the system is loaded."
msgstr "Funnel パラメータは揃いました。ID の右欄に構造の VMD ID を入れます。Main Menu の構造一覧の左にあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:95
msgid ""
"Once the system in VMD has been selected, it is possible to provide a group "
"of atoms that will be used to compute the center of mass (COM) of the ligand"
" using the VMD syntax. Depending on the ligand's structure it could be best "
"to provide a subselection of atoms, but in our example we will just get all "
"heavy atoms of benzamidine by typing:"
msgstr ""
"VMD 構文で Ligand COM の原子群を指定します。構造により部分選択がよい場合もありますが、今回は Benzamidine の全 Heavy "
"Atom を次で選びます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:100
msgid ""
"By clicking on 'Apply' a first draft of the PLUMED input should appear, "
"containing all parameters set up until now by the user. It is possible to "
"see few empty variables that must be completed before launching the "
"simulation."
msgstr "Apply で入力案が表示されます。未記入変数は実行前に埋めます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:102
msgid ""
"This can be done using the drop-down menu. Here, it is possible to select "
"the remaining simulation parameters and type in the box at the right the "
"value for each parameter; press ‘Enter’ and then ‘Apply’ to update the "
"PLUMED input with the new data. We suggest reading the protocol paper for a "
"better description of every single option. In general, all fields with a "
"'<fill>' or '<?>' flag need to be specified with a user-defined value or "
"file, respectively, before running the simulation."
msgstr ""
"Drop-down で残りのパラメータを選び、右欄に値を入れ、Enter・Apply で更新します。各オプションは Protocol "
"論文を参照してください。<fill> は値、<?> はファイルをユーザーが指定する欄です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:105
msgid ""
"The canvas where the PLUMED input is outputted can also be modified "
"manually, however this should be done as last thing because clicking 'Apply'"
" would reset any manual change."
msgstr "入力欄は手動変更もできますが、Apply が消してしまうため最後に行ってください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:107
msgid ""
"To print the file, it is possible to click on 'Export' and 'Export for "
"Plumed' to create a text file with all the information written in the "
"interface canvas."
msgstr "Export、Export for Plumed で表示内容を Text File に出力します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:109
msgid ""
"TO BE NOTED: at this point the file is still lacking collective variables "
"(CVs) for the metadynamics. The user should add fitting candidates depending"
" on the system and problem at hand. In our case, a simple distance between "
"the COM of benzamidine and a selection of atoms in the binding pocket of "
"trypsin should suffice."
msgstr ""
"注意：Metadynamics の CV はまだありません。系と問題に合う CV を加えます。ここでは Benzamidine COM と "
"Trypsin Pocket の原子群間距離で十分です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:111
msgid ""
"The last step in using the VMD interface involves the creation of a "
"reference pdb file from the target structure used to set up the funnel-shape"
" potential. This file will be used for the alignment of the target structure"
" when the metadynamics bias is added to the system and should be added at "
"the 'REFERENCE' flag in FUNNEL_PS. It should contain only atoms of the "
"target molecule or a selection of them. It is strongly suggested that the "
"backbone atoms of secondary structures (i.e., alpha helix and beta sheet) be"
" chosen."
msgstr ""
"最後に、Funnel 設定に使った標的の参照 PDB を作ります。Bias を加えた際の標的の重ね合わせに使い、FUNNEL_PS の "
"REFERENCE に指定します。標的の全原子または部分集合だけを含めます。Secondary Structure（Alpha-helix、Beta-"
"sheet）の Backbone を強く推奨します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:113
msgid ""
"TO BE NOTED: beware when creating such a file with VMD since the final "
"structure may have atoms renumbered, and this could create a mismatch during"
" the simulation, causing artifacts and crashes."
msgstr "注意：VMD の出力で原子番号が変わると、不一致により Artifact や Crash を招くため確認してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:115
msgid ""
"For users that opted to follow the VMD plug-in route, it is possible to skip"
" directly to the simulation phase. Following, we are going to explain how to"
" use the Funnel Metadynamics Pre-Processing Tool web server."
msgstr "VMD で準備した場合は実行編へ進めます。以下は Web Server の説明です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:117
msgid "Access the server [website](https://mbuto.si.usi.ch/)."
msgstr "Server の [Web サイト](https://mbuto.si.usi.ch/) にアクセスします。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:119
msgid ""
"Create an account to access the service and log in with the credentials."
msgstr "Account を作成して Login します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:121
msgid ""
"Create a new 'Discovery' by clicking the plus on the upper left side of the "
"interface and give it a name. This information will remain stored for a "
"certain amount of time in case it is necessary to retrieve the project and "
"change few parameters. Press 'Add' to finalize the creation of the "
"discovery."
msgstr "左上の Plus で新しい Discovery に名前を付け、Add で作成します。一定期間保存されるため、再取得して変更できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:123
msgid ""
"Load the structure of your interest by fetching a particular PDBID or by "
"uploading the file of your system. The user can click on secondary "
"structures to zoom the view and, by shift+left-clicking, show atoms in a "
"radius of the selected residue. A violet color signals the selected residue "
"and the user can press numbers from 1 to 8 to adjust the zone to display "
"atoms."
msgstr ""
"PDBID で取得するかファイルを Upload します。Secondary Structure をクリックして "
"Zoom、Shift+左クリックで選択残基周囲の原子を表示します。選択は紫色で、1〜8キーで表示範囲を変えられます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:125
msgid ""
"Start defining the funnel shape by clicking on the funnel icon on the left "
"(named 'Funnel'). A set of options will be displayed on the right, which can"
" be set interactively."
msgstr "左の Funnel アイコンを押すと右にオプションが出ます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:127
msgid ""
"Definition of the parameters follows the same rationale of the VMD plug in "
"(points 1 to 17). Following, we will just specify the procedure."
msgstr "意味は VMD の手順1〜17と同じなので、操作だけ示します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:129
msgid ""
"Point A and B can be chosen by clicking on atoms, specifying the value of a "
"given coordinate, or by adapting the value with the arrows in the boxes."
msgstr "A・B は原子のクリック、座標入力、矢印で選びます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:131
msgid ""
"Zcc is in the form of a slider, taking as a reference the point A. Alpha and"
" Rcyl can be changed by providing directly a value or with the arrows and "
"they are expressed in radians and Å, respectively."
msgstr "Zcc は A を基準に Slider で指定します。Alpha は radian、Rcyl は Å で、直接入力か矢印を使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:133
msgid ""
"The ANCHOR point is selected by first flagging the checkbox on the left of "
"'Anchor point' and then clicking on an atom of the interface. Remember to "
"uncheck the box to avoid changing the ANCHOR point by error when the "
"selection is done. When an atom has been selected, its serial number should "
"appear on the right of the option, signaling that an atom has been correctly"
" provided."
msgstr ""
"Anchor point の左の Checkbox を入れて原子をクリックし、選択後は誤変更を防ぐため解除します。右に Serial Number "
"が出れば設定できています。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:135
msgid ""
"It is possible to undisplay or display the Funnel by clicking on the eye on "
"the top right of the interface."
msgstr "右上の目で Funnel 表示を切り替えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:137
msgid ""
"Switch to the 'Bounds' section on the left panel to start defining the walls"
" and upper and lower limits that will be applied in the FM simulation."
msgstr "左の Bounds で Wall と上下限を設定します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:139
msgid ""
"In the web server, the walls and limits are defined with sliders and they "
"are represented by discs, clearly defining their boundaries with respect to "
"point A. The web server has also an internal check to warn the user if "
"improper values of bounds have been selected. In this case, a red message "
"will be displayed on the side of the wrong parameter."
msgstr "Slider で指定し、A に対する境界を円盤で表示します。不適切な値は右に赤い警告が出ます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:141
msgid ""
"A new feature of the web server is the possibility to define geometric "
"collective variables that can be added directly in the PLUMED input at the "
"end of the procedure. To do so, switch to the 'Collective variables' panel "
"on the left that has a wrench as symbol."
msgstr ""
"Server では幾何学 CV を定義して入力に直接追加できます。左の Wrench アイコンの Collective variables を開きます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:143
msgid ""
"A list of user-defined collective variables can be found on the upper right "
"of the interface. To date, it is possible to set a distance, angle, or "
"dihedral angle and the system will automatically recognize the type of CV "
"based on the user interaction. By right-clicking with the mouse on atoms the"
" system will start to store their information and right-clicking again on "
"the same atom stops the procedure. Thus, if the user right-clicks on two "
"atoms and stops the selection there by right-clicking again on the second "
"atom, a distance will be defined."
msgstr ""
"右上に定義済み CV があります。距離・角・Dihedral "
"を操作から自動判定します。原子を右クリックして順に選び、同じ原子を再度右クリックして終了します。例えば2原子を選んで2番目を再クリックすると距離です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:145
msgid ""
"It is also possible to define centers of mass (COM) to be used with the "
"geometrical CVs. To do so, check the box on the left of CV virtual Atom and "
"start selecting atoms with the left-click of the mouse. A red sphere should "
"show the position of the COM in the Cartesian space and it updates for each "
"new selection. When the user is satisfied in selecting the correct number of"
" atoms, a click on the plus on the right of the interface finalizes the "
"selection and stops the process to start a new COM definition."
msgstr ""
"COM も定義できます。CV virtual Atom の左を Check し、左クリックで原子を選ぶと赤球の COM が更新されます。右の Plus "
"で確定し、次の COM の定義に移ります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:147
msgid ""
"A 'History Log' is accessible on the left panel by clicking on the "
"homonymous option (clock symbol). Here the user can revert a move or restore"
" a previous state in the definition of parameters."
msgstr "左の時計アイコンの History Log で操作を戻し、以前の設定を復元できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:149
msgid ""
"Once all the parameters have been set, it is possible to create the PLUMED "
"input file. To do so, click on the 'Protein' option at the top of the left "
"panel (symbolized by atoms) and click on the 'PLUMED FILE' button on the "
"right of the interface. A window should pop up with boxes to define the "
"final values to complete the input and a drop-down menu to select particular"
" CVs if any have been defined. It is also possible to create the pdb file to"
" provide to the REFERENCE flag in FUNNEL_PS, although we suggest the user to"
" adapt this file to the system under study as explained in the reference "
"[protocol](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41596-020-0342-4)."
msgstr ""
"全設定後、左上の Protein（原子アイコン）、右の PLUMED FILE を押します。最終値の欄と、定義した CV の選択 Menu "
"が開きます。FUNNEL_PS の REFERENCE 用 PDB "
"も作れますが、[Protocol](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41596-020-0342-4) "
"に従い系に合わせて調整してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:151
msgid "Press the 'DOWNLOAD' button to obtain a PLUMED input file."
msgstr "DOWNLOAD で PLUMED 入力を取得します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:153
msgid ""
"The procedure of pre-processing is now terminated and the user can progress "
"to the Simulation phase. In case of bugs, please contact the email address "
"andreabritesma@gmail.com."
msgstr "前処理は終了です。実行編へ進めます。不具合は andreabritesma@gmail.com に連絡してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:156
msgid "Simulation"
msgstr "シミュレーション"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:158
msgid ""
"This part of the tutorial is elective and, depepnding on the system under "
"study and hardware, it could require some simulation time. For this reason, "
"we provide files that could be used by the user to skip directly to the "
"post-processing exercise."
msgstr "実行は任意で、系・Hardware により時間がかかります。解析に直接進めるファイルも用意しています。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:161
msgid "For the following exercise, we are going to use GROMACS."
msgstr "次の演習は GROMACS を使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:163
msgid ""
"To launch a FM simulation, launch a normal simulation in GROMACS adding the "
"flag '-plumed' followed by the name of the file prepared in the pre-"
"processing exercise. Depending on the version and configuration of GROMACS "
"in your machine, the command input might slightly change."
msgstr "通常の GROMACS コマンドに -plumed と前処理で作ったファイル名を加えます。バージョン・設定で多少異なります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:165
msgid "For GROMACS-5.1.4+PLUMED-2.6:"
msgstr "GROMACS-5.1.4+PLUMED-2.6 の場合："

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:169
msgid "For GROMACS-2020.6+PLUMED-2.7.1 (serial version):"
msgstr "GROMACS-2020.6+PLUMED-2.7.1（逐次版）："

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:173
msgid "For GROMACS-2020.6+PLUMED-2.7.1 (MPI version):"
msgstr "GROMACS-2020.6+PLUMED-2.7.1（MPI 版）："

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:178
msgid ""
"Check that the files 'HILLS', 'COLVAR' and 'BIAS' are created. The 'BIAS' "
"file contains the information of the funnel-shape restraint potential."
msgstr "HILLS、COLVAR、BIAS の生成を確認します。BIAS は Funnel Restraint の情報です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:180
msgid ""
"Stop the FM simulation once the free-energy calculation reaches convergence."
" To check the convergence, compute the binding free-energy surface (BFES) as"
" a function of the simulation time. This operation can be done while the "
"simulation is ongoing using the command:"
msgstr "自由エネルギーが収束したら止めます。結合自由エネルギー表面 (BFES) の時間変化を、実行中でも次で調べられます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:184
msgid ""
"As a rule of thumb, the calculation is converged if the system continues "
"exploring the bound and unbound state in the CV space, while the computed "
"BFES as a function of the time does not change significantly."
msgstr "目安は、結合・非結合の両状態を探索し続け、BFES が時間とともに大きく変わらないことです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:186
msgid ""
"TO BE NOTED: the simulation time to converge in the calculation is variable "
"and depends on several factors, such as the size of the system, the number "
"and types of CVs and metadynamics parameters. In the case of "
"benzamidine–trypsin, the calculation converged after 250 ns. This check can "
"be done with the help of the post-processing interface if necessary (see "
"point X in post-processing exercise)."
msgstr ""
"注意：収束時間は系の大きさ、CV の数・種類、パラメータに依存します。Benzamidine–Trypsin は250 ns で収束しました。後処理 "
"GUI でも確認できます（後処理演習の手順 X）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:188
msgid "Post-processing exercise"
msgstr "後処理演習"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:190
msgid ""
"In case the user did not run the simulation, we provide sample files "
"start.pdb and trj.trr to load a strided FM simulation, the HILLS file of the"
" simulation, a number of binding free-energy surfaces (BFES), and a COLVAR "
"file already strided."
msgstr ""
"未実行の場合用に、間引いた Trajectory の start.pdb・trj.trr、HILLS、複数 BFES、間引き済み COLVAR "
"を用意しています。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:192
msgid ""
"The user can follow the procedure through the following numbered points and "
"the graphical user interface FFS. Additionally, a notebook (Solution.ipynb) "
"is provided in the github folder, which contains the most important "
"calculations inside the tool."
msgstr "以下の手順と FFS GUI を使えます。主要計算を含む Solution.ipynb も GitHub にあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:194
msgid ""
"Open VMD and load the trajectory produced by the simulation in the "
"Simulation exercise. This can be done by loading xtc + gro, or crd + prmtop,"
" or dcd + pdb files for example (users will find start.pdb and trj.trr in "
"data/post-processing)."
msgstr ""
"VMD に Trajectory を読みます。例えば xtc+gro、crd+prmtop、dcd+pdb です。data/post-"
"processing に start.pdb・trj.trr があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:196
msgid ""
"Source the plug-in ffs.tcl to start the analysis of the FM trajectory. To do"
" so, go to Extension->Tk console on the Main window of VMD, type"
msgstr "Main の Extension->Tk console で ffs.tcl を Source します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:200
msgid "and then"
msgstr "続いて、"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:204
msgid "The post-processing GUI should now be visible."
msgstr "後処理 GUI が表示されます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:206
msgid ""
"TO BE NOTED: in case the tooltip library was not loaded beforehand, please "
"follow indications in point 1 of the pre-processing exercise before sourcing"
" ffs.tcl."
msgstr "注意：tooltip 未読み込みなら、ffs.tcl の前に前処理の手順1に従ってください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:208
msgid ""
"Two post-processing calculations are available. The first allows the "
"calculation of the BFES through the PLUMED-2 'sum_hills' command. This is "
"used for one of the convergence checks routinely done on metadynamics "
"calculations and to reconstruct the BFES as a function of the CVs used in "
"the simulation. The second option uses the PLUMED-2 'driver' command to "
"provide values of CVs, rescale potentials, and much more along the "
"simulation trajectory. We will start describing the first option. You can "
"find the second option from point 9."
msgstr ""
"2つの計算があります。sum_hills は CV の BFES を再構成し、収束を確認します。driver は Trajectory の "
"CV・Potential の Rescale などを計算します。まず前者を説明し、後者は手順9からです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:212
msgid ""
"Click the 'Plumed (bin)' button and select the folder path to the binary "
"file 'plumed' of PLUMED-2 on the user’s computer. The name of the selected "
"file is shown to the right of the button."
msgstr "Plumed (bin) で PLUMED-2 の実行ファイル plumed を選びます。右に名前が出ます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:214
msgid ""
"Click the 'Hills' button and select the folder path to the 'HILLS' file "
"produced in Step 1 of the 'Simulation' phase. Alternatively, the user can "
"load the HILLS_800ns provided inside the github folder."
msgstr "Hills で実行編の HILLS、または GitHub の HILLS_800ns を選びます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:216
msgid ""
"Decide whether to use the lowest energy minimum as the ground state (0 "
"kJ/mol state) through the ‘Min to zero?’ drop-down menu. This operation "
"facilitates the comparison between states and has no consequence on the "
"computation of the BFES."
msgstr "Min to zero? で最小を0 kJ/mol にするか選びます。比較が楽になり、BFES 計算には影響しません。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:218
msgid ""
"Specify the value of the product between the Boltzmann constant and the "
"temperature in kJ/mol (e.g., 2.479 at 298 K)."
msgstr "Boltzmann 定数×温度を kJ/mol で指定します。298 K なら2.479です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:220
msgid ""
"Click the ‘Output’ button and select the folder in which you prefer to save "
"the output files. The folder name appears to the right of the button."
msgstr "Output で保存先を選ぶと右に表示されます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:222
msgid ""
"Click 'RUN Sum_hills LR' to compute the BFES using a small bin number (150 "
"points per CV). This is recommended to avoid computer cache memory issues "
"when plotting the BFES in the FMAP GUI (Step 16). Alternatively, click 'RUN "
"Sum_hills HR' to compute the BFES using a larger bin number, which is useful"
" for the accurate estimate of the ligand binding free energy (Step 19). You "
"can produce several BFESs computed along the simulation time by clicking "
"'RUN Sum_hills stride'. The number of BFESs produced depends on the stride "
"value specified in the 'stride' entry. 'RUN Sum_hills stride' is useful for "
"the convergence control and the binding free-energy calculation (Step 20). "
"In all the cases, wait until the calculation is complete. The output of "
"sum_hills is displayed in the VMD tk console; thus, you can check the "
"progress of the calculation."
msgstr ""
"RUN Sum_hills LR は CV ごと150点の低解像度で、FMAP GUI の描画時の Cache "
"問題を避けるため推奨します（手順16）。HR は高解像度で結合自由エネルギーの高精度推定に有用です（手順19）。stride は指定間隔で時間ごとの "
"BFES を作り、収束確認・結合自由エネルギーに使います（手順20）。終了まで待ち、VMD Tk Console の出力で進捗を確認します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:224
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can use the interface to perform a driver calculation. "
"Skip to step 16 to continue the analysis of the BFESs."
msgstr "driver も Interface から使えます。BFES 解析の続きは手順16へ進んでください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:226
msgid ""
"Click the ‘Plumed (bin)’ button and select the folder path to the binary "
"file 'plumed' of PLUMED-2 on the user’s computer. The name of the selected "
"file is shown to the right of the button."
msgstr "Plumed (bin) で PLUMED-2 の実行ファイル plumed を選びます。右に名前が出ます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:228
msgid ""
"Prepare a PLUMED-2 input file using a text editor and specify the CVs for "
"which the statistics along the simulation should be computed. To load the "
"file, click the 'Input (.dat)' button. The name of the selected file is "
"shown to the right of the button."
msgstr "Text Editor で統計を計算する CV の PLUMED-2 入力を作り、Input (.dat) で読みます。右に名前が出ます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:230
msgid ""
"Click the 'Trajectory' button to select the trajectory on which the Driver "
"command should run."
msgstr "Trajectory で driver の対象を選びます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:232
msgid ""
"TO BE NOTED: the full (not strided) trajectory of the simulation produced at"
" Step 1 of the 'Simulation' phase should be used."
msgstr "注意：実行編の手順1で生成した、間引いていない全 Trajectory を使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:234
msgid ""
"Specify the trajectory format depending on the program used for the FM "
"simulation (i.e., .xtc or .trr for GROMACS, .dcd for NAMD and .crd for "
"Amber, respectively) by using the drop-down menu to the right of 'Trajectory"
" extension'."
msgstr ""
"Trajectory extension の右で形式を選びます。GROMACS は .xtc/.trr、NAMD は .dcd、Amber は .crd"
" です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:236
msgid ""
"Click the 'Pdb file' button and specify the .pdb file of the system "
"associated to the trajectory. In this file, the occupancy and beta-factor "
"columns should be replaced with the mass and charge of each atom, "
"respectively, especially if the collective variable (CV) computed employs "
"calculations dependent on either of them."
msgstr ""
"Pdb file で対応する PDB を指定します。特に質量・電荷依存 CV では、occupancy と beta-factor "
"を各原子の質量・電荷に置き換えてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:238
msgid ""
"Click the 'Output' button and select the folder in which you prefer to save "
"the output files."
msgstr "Output で保存先を選びます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:240
msgid ""
"Click 'RUN Driver' and wait until the calculation is completed. The "
"calculation output of driver is displayed in the VMD tk console, allowing "
"you to check the progress of the calculation."
msgstr "RUN Driver で実行し、終了を待ちます。Tk Console で進捗を確認できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:242
msgid ""
"Plot the BFES of the system using the ‘Plot FES’ button. You can plot the "
"BFES created at Step 8 or any other FES in the PLUMED-2 format. You can plot"
" both 1D and 2D FESs. As reported in Step 8, for this task we recommend "
"creating the FES using 'RUN Sum_hills LR' to avoid computer cash memory "
"issues."
msgstr ""
"Plot FES で手順8または任意の PLUMED-2 形式の1次元・2次元 BFES を表示します。Cache 問題を避けるため LR "
"の使用を推奨します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:244
msgid ""
"The user can scroll the frames of the simulation trajectory loaded at Step "
"11 and visualize at the same time their position in the BFES produced at "
"Step 25 by clicking the 'Trace' button. To make this option active, click "
"'Output' and select the folder path to the 'COLVAR' file. The COLVAR file "
"should have the same number of frames of the simulation trajectory. To "
"ensure this is the case, if you have not already, create the COLVAR file "
"from the trajectory loaded in VMD using 'Driver' as shown from step 9 to 15."
" Otherwise, a COLVAR file with the same number of frames of trj.trr is "
"provided in the github folder."
msgstr ""
"Trace で、読み込んだ Trajectory（手順11）の Frame と BFES（手順25）上の位置を同時に追えます。Output で "
"COLVAR を選びます。Frame 数を一致させるため、必要なら手順9〜15の Driver で VMD の Trajectory "
"から作ります。trj.trr と同数の COLVAR も GitHub にあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:247
msgid ""
"You can extract the system structures belonging to a selected region in the "
"BFES (i.e., the binding poses at the lowest free-energy minimum). To do so, "
"click 'Output' and specify the folder path to the 'COLVAR' file that has the"
" same number of frames of the trajectory. If the file is missing, follow "
"Step 9 to create a new 'COLVAR' file. Then, hold the right button of the "
"mouse drawing a selection area in the displayed BFES (depending on your OS "
"the keybind might change). A pop-up message is displayed to inform the user "
"about the number of structures that will be extracted. A new folder called "
"'Selected_structures' is automatically created including the pdb file for "
"each frame extracted. The pdb files are named after the frame number, and a "
"log file reports the list of frame numbers that were extracted. "
"Alternatively, the same result is obtained by typing the CV interval of "
"interest in the FES in the boxes to the right ('min_x' 'max_x'; 'min_y' "
"'max_y') and clicking 'Extract'. If the displayed FES is 1D, use only the "
"first two boxes ('min_x' and 'max_x'); in the case of 2D FESs, all four "
"fields should be filled ('min_x', 'max_x', 'min_y' and 'max_y')."
msgstr ""
"BFES の指定領域（最小付近の結合 Pose など）の構造を抽出できます。Output で同じ Frame 数の COLVAR "
"を指定し、なければ手順9で作ります。BFES 上を右 Drag して選択します（OS "
"で操作は異なります）。抽出数の通知後、Selected_structures に Frame 番号の PDB と一覧 Log "
"が生成されます。代わりに右の min_x・max_x、2次元なら min_y・max_y も入れ、Extract "
"を押せます。1次元は最初の2欄だけ、2次元は4欄すべてを使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:249
msgid ""
"Calculate the absolute protein–ligand binding free energy. To do so, first "
"type the CV interval identifying the bound state in the boxes introduced at "
"Step 18 ('min_x' and 'max_x' in the case of 1D BFES; 'min_x', 'max_x', "
"'min_y' and 'max_y' in the case of 2D BFES). Looking at the BFES, type in "
"'Wref value at' the reference CV value for the unbound state (i.e., the "
"ligand is far from the protein and the BFES is flat). Specify the radius of "
"the cylinder section used during the FM simulation and click 'Calculate!'. "
"The GUI will ask for a BFES file for the calculation. You can provide either"
" the BFES generated by 'RUN Sum_hills LR' at Step 8 or a new BFES calculated"
" by clicking 'RUN Sum_hills HR', which might lead to a more accurate "
"estimate of the ligand binding free energy. Unlike when executing the "
"previous commands, the calculation output is not displayed in the VMD "
"terminal; instead, the final value is shown in kcal/mol to the right of the "
"'Calculate!' button. This estimate already includes the entropy correction "
"due to the presence of the funnel-shape potential."
msgstr ""
"絶対 Protein-Ligand 結合自由エネルギーを求めます。結合領域を1次元なら min_x・max_x、2次元なら min_y・max_y "
"も指定します。Wref value at に、Ligand が遠く BFES が平坦な非結合参照 CV を入れます。Cylinder 半径を指定し "
"Calculate! を押し、BFES を選びます。LR でも使えますが、HR で再計算すると精度が上がる場合があります。結果は Terminal "
"ではなくボタン右に kcal/mol で表示し、Funnel による Entropy 補正を含みます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:253
msgid ""
"The user can compute the ligand binding free energy and its standard "
"deviation as a function of the simulation time. This operation is useful to "
"assess the convergence of the FM calculation. Practically, the ligand "
"binding free energy and its s.d. are estimated generating several BFESs "
"computed as time-weighted average along the simulation. The BFES files can "
"be created in Step 8. Select the folder where all the BFESs are stored by "
"clicking the 'Output' button. Type the CV interval identifying the bound "
"state and the reference CV value for the unbound state as done in Step 18. "
"Finally, type the radius of the cylinder section used during the FM "
"simulation and click 'Convergence'. At the end of the job, a graph of the "
"binding free-energy difference as a function of the serial number of BFES is"
" displayed. At the same time, the value of the freeenergy difference with "
"the corresponding s.d. computed from each BFES is reported in the tk_console"
" of VMD."
msgstr ""
"結合自由エネルギーと標準偏差の時間変化で収束を評価できます。手順8で時間加重平均の BFES を複数作り、Output "
"で保存先を指定します。結合領域、非結合参照 CV、Cylinder 半径を入れ、Convergence を押します。BFES "
"番号に対する差の図が開き、各差と s.d. が VMD Tk Console に出ます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:255
msgid ""
"At the beginning of the simulation, the free-energy calculation has not "
"converged yet; therefore, the graph obtained in Step 20 typically shows "
"large fluctuations. The user can exclude this part of the simulation from "
"the computation of the graph in Step 20 by typing the number of frames to "
"discard in the field on the right of 'Rej. Time' (reject time). Then, repeat"
" Step 20 to recompute the ligand binding free energy and its s.d. without "
"considering the initial part of the simulation. The 'Rej. Time' can be "
"easily defined by looking at the graph generated in Step 20 and identifying "
"the converged part in the binding free-energy graph that shows lower "
"fluctuations around a given value."
msgstr ""
"初期の未収束部分は大きく揺らぎます。Rej. Time の右に除外する Frame 数を入れ、手順20を繰り返して平均・s.d. "
"を再計算します。一定値の周囲で揺らぎが小さくなる収束部分を図から選びます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:258
msgid ""
"In addition to Step 21, the user can check the convergence of the FM "
"calculation through a block bootstrap analysis performed by clicking the "
"button 'Block bootstrap'. Once you have defined the 'Rej. Time' as shown in "
"Step 21, the remaining simulation frames are divided in ten blocks, and for "
"each of them a bootstrap analysis is performed. The user obtains the "
"estimation of the mean of the binding free energy and its standard error and"
" a histogram representation of the values distribution for each block. The "
"user should check that the distributions are Gaussian like. The convergence "
"of the calculation is reached when the values of the binding free energy "
"computed in the last blocks are very close (i.e., their difference is <1 "
"kcal/mol). We note that the binding free-energy value computed in the last "
"block should be very similar to that computed in Step 21."
msgstr ""
"さらに Block bootstrap で確認できます。Rej. Time 後の Frame を10 Block に分け、各々 Bootstrap "
"し、結合自由エネルギー平均・標準誤差・分布 Histogram を得ます。分布が Gaussian に似ることを確認します。最後の Block "
"間の差が1 kcal/mol 未満なら収束とします。最後の値は手順21とほぼ同じになるはずです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:261
msgid ""
"At this point the user should have achieved convergence and the value "
"provided from the last point in the weighted avergae can be reported as the "
"result of FM for the system under study."
msgstr "収束したら、Weighted Average の最後の値を FM 結果として報告できます。"
